. evidence/lib.sh
UUID=86d7dc8e-3373-47af-86dd-56a1cd517e2f
ev_verdict D-5 PASS "From the Linux VM (Firefox 157 plus Duo Desktop 4.7.0 under emulation) the sign-in to the Duo demo ended with trusted_endpoint_status trusted, auth_result allow (Login Successful), device_info_source duo_desktop, endpoint EPBXQCG5T0RRF1PNK3QE. The second factor was a bypass code (the test user's only enrolled factor is Touch ID on the Mac). The browser asked for the local-network permission first. See 06-3-after-local-network-allow.png and 10-7-auth-response-bottom.png."
ev_init L-1 "Linux device ID: Duo Desktop, Fleet and the CSV agree" "The ID Duo matches for a Linux host is its product UUID, which equals Fleet's host UUID and the row in linux.csv." "Same value in all four places; Duo marks the endpoint trusted." >/dev/null
ev_vm L-1 on-the-host "echo \"product_uuid: \$(cat /sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid)\"; echo \"machine-id : \$(cat /etc/machine-id)  (the fallback Duo Desktop 4.7.0+ uses only if no product UUID exists, formatted as a UUID)\"" >/dev/null
ev_cmd L-1 in-fleet-and-in-the-csv "echo \"Fleet host uuid : \$(fleetctl api '/hosts/identifier/$UUID' 2>/dev/null | jq -r .host.uuid)\"; echo \"linux.csv row    : \$(tail -1 duo/run/linux.csv)\"; echo \"Sync cache      : \$(grep 'linux:' duo/sync.log | tail -1)\"" >/dev/null
ev_note L-1 "Duo's side: the D-5 Auth Response (screenshots 06 to 07 in the D-5 folder) shows device_info_source duo_desktop and trusted_endpoint_status trusted for this host. Duo's admin endpoint record (Trusted Endpoint: Yes, via device health) was read earlier from the Admin Panel; a fresh capture needs the admin to sign in again."
ev_verdict L-1 PASS "product_uuid = Fleet host UUID = linux.csv row = 86d7dc8e-3373-47af-86dd-56a1cd517e2f, and Duo marked the endpoint trusted. Case matched (lowercase). The /etc/machine-id fallback is not used because this VM exposes a product UUID. L-2 (a VM without one) was not tested."
